From: alvesmaicon <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: sun8i-codec-analog: let the headphone amplifier settle before powering down

With headphones on the jack (direct drive, the return on HPCOM), every
stream end popped loudly and reset the whole analog block: headphone
volume back to 0, the PA source mutes and every other analog control
back to its default, while the driver kept no cache to notice.

DAPM powers the path down right after the headphone amplifier: the DAC,
HPCOM and the clocks within a few ms. Spacing those steps showed that
the reset stops once the amplifier has 300 ms to itself, and the pop
once it has about 800 ms. Wait 1 s after it goes off.

diff --git a/sound/soc/sunxi/sun8i-codec-analog.c b/sound/soc/sunxi/sun8i-codec-analog.c
index 2024e2b..238f989 100644
--- a/sound/soc/sunxi/sun8i-codec-analog.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sunxi/sun8i-codec-analog.c
@@ -359,6 +359,13 @@ static int sun8i_headphone_amp_event(struct snd_soc_dapm_widget *w,
 		snd_soc_component_update_bits(component, SUN8I_ADDA_PAEN_HP_CTRL,
 					      BIT(SUN8I_ADDA_PAEN_HP_CTRL_HPPAEN),
 					      0x0);
+		/*
+		 * Let the amplifier's output settle before the rest of the
+		 * path (DAC, HPCOM, clocks) powers down: with headphones on
+		 * the jack, powering it all down at once pops and resets the
+		 * analog block, volumes and mutes back to their defaults.
+		 */
+		msleep(1000);
 	}
 
 	return 0;
